cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HealthFraudML: Open-Source Healthcare Fraud Detection Framework"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bahudhoddi"
    given-names: "Bharath Kumar"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0118-7428"
    affiliation: "University of the Cumberlands"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bharath309/healthfraudml"
url: "https://github.com/bharath309/healthfraudml"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.1
abstract: >-
  HealthFraudML is a modular Python framework for healthcare claims fraud
  detection. It provides a unified API over supervised, unsupervised and hybrid
  machine-learning models; fraud-type detectors for upcoding, unbundling,
  duplicate claims and phantom billing; a rule-based patient billing auditor
  that flags upcoding, unbundling and charges far above a disclosed review
  threshold, and drafts a dispute letter; and an organizational readiness
  assessment. Explanations for flagged cases are derived from each model's own
  feature importances; SHAP and LIME are not used by the package. The
  repository ships a price benchmark of 7,359 separately payable CPT/HCPCS
  codes derived from the public CMS Physician Fee Schedule Relative Value File
  (PPRRVU25_JAN.csv, conversion factor 32.3465), carrying code numbers and CMS
  national payment amounts only; no AMA CPT descriptors are distributed. The
  identity-theft detector is a stub that always returns no findings, no
  kickback detector exists, and the anonymization module does not provide a
  k-anonymity guarantee.
keywords:
  - healthcare fraud detection
  - machine learning
  - medical billing
  - claims analysis
  - explainable AI
  - CMS Physician Fee Schedule
  - Python
